{
  "abstract": "A thin wrapper that exposes, with Mathlib definitions only, the basic recolouring lemmas of edge-colouring theory proved inside PALOMAR-2026-11-04-000009 (overfull-critical-graphs). vizing_adjacency_lemma (Vizing 1965): if G is of class two (its line graph is not Δ(G)-colourable) and G − xy is Δ(G)-edge-colourable, then x has at least Δ − d(y) + 1 neighbours of degree Δ other than y. critical_two_maxDegree_neighbours: every vertex of a Δ-critical graph has at least two neighbours of degree Δ. multifan_lemma (Stiebitz–Scheide–Toft–Favrholdt, Theorem 2.1): for a Δ(G)-colouring of G − x y₀ of a class-two graph, a multifan at x is elementary and x is joined to every fan vertex by a path coloured with any colour free at x and any colour free at that vertex. kierstead_lemma (Kierstead 1984): a Kierstead path whose interior vertices y₂, …, y_{L−2} have degree below Δ is elementary. Partial edge colourings are symmetric functions V → V → Option (Fin k); five definitions (proper partial edge colouring, colouring of G − ab, free colour, multifan, Kierstead path). The only new proof is the corollary (from Vizing's lemma) and the translation to the colourings of the Vizing entry.",
